# Feature Workflow

Repeatable process for adding a feature to the HMS frontend.

## Requirements

- Start by identifying route, state, data needs, validation, localization, responsive behavior, and tests.
- Create the feature folder with the standard `data/domain/presentation` structure.
- Define domain models and repository contracts before wiring UI to real data when non-trivial.
- Add localization keys before adding user-facing text.
- Reuse shared components before creating feature-specific widgets.
- Queue/workspace features must confirm layout against [`ui-workspace.mdc`](./ui-workspace.mdc) and a reference module first.
- Confirm subscription-gated access and permission gates before exposing routes or actions ([`permissions.mdc`](./permissions.mdc)).
- Verify mobile, tablet, and desktop layouts; must not hard-code colors, spacing, or typography ([`design-system.mdc`](./design-system.mdc)).
- Reference entities by `human_friendly_id`; must not expose raw table IDs.
- Enforce RBAC+ABAC visibility for menus, components, and actions.
- Shared-data mutations must update Riverpod immediately and reconcile via [`instant_ui_sync.mdc`](./instant_ui_sync.mdc).
- Add tests for controller logic, repository mapping, and important widgets.
- Update docs when structure or conventions change.

## Acceptance

- The feature works at supported breakpoints with no boundary violations.
- Queue screens match [`ui-workspace.mdc`](./ui-workspace.mdc) when applicable.
- Tests and localization are included.

